Subject: [PATCH 06851/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): re86 + sc25 honest nulls,
 both with real progress

Continuation of round-3.

re86: L7 wall holds, but the full color assignment is now decoded (the
37px plus -> four color-8 sockets, the small plus -> three color-11
sockets after deformation, the rectangle -> 19x7 for two color-9
sockets, including a previously-overlooked fourth color-8 socket). An
early wrong assignment and a repaint-swatch trap burned the per-level
move bar before the live attempt timed out. A future attempt can route
directly to the known assignment instead of re-discovering it.

sc25: directly answers v19's own recommendation from round 2 (find a way
to conserve energy on the final approach). Found the prior 42-label
partial's two opening cross casts are unnecessary -- cutting them saves
12 energy (42 vs 30 remaining), exactly the margin the last two sessions
were missing at the doorstep. This run got trapped in a newly-identified
southwest-socket dead end instead (repeated B casts lock to that pad
once occupied) -- a known trap to route around next time, not an
unknown. No new level banked in either game; reproducible_total_levels
stays 143.

